VEForAll extension

Version 0.6

Pierre Boutet, Clément Flipo, Ike Hecht, Yaron Koren, Cindy Cicalese

VEForAll ("VisualEditor For All") is a MediaWiki extension that provides
the ability for other extensions to make use of VisualEditor within
textareas. VEForAll does not do anything on its own; rather, it defines a
JavaScript function, applyVisualEditor(), which can be called on any
textarea input.

As you might expect, the VisualEditor extension must be installed for VEForAll
to work.

For more information, see the extension homepage at:
https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Extension:VEForAll

Wikidebates integration (MediaWiki 1.43)
----------------------------------------

The former stand-alone VEForAllMobileDeps extension has been integrated into
this fork. On Minerva, VEForAll registers its scoped mobile-toolbar CSS
through ext.veforall.main, rather than loading it on ordinary read pages.
The mobile VE bundles are declared as ResourceLoader dependencies of
ext.veforall.core.mobile and are requested on first editor visibility/focus
instead of being preloaded on every mobile page.

The modules are ext.visualEditor.core.mobile and ext.visualEditor.mwcore, in
addition to ext.veforall.core. Other dependencies such as targetLoader,
mediawiki and base are provided by the existing module dependency graph.
The old name ext.visualEditor.mobile is not present in MW 1.43 and has
deliberately not been copied. The old empty mobileFix.css and unused
mobileFix.js marker are not needed.

After the farm pins a version of VEForAll containing this integration, remove
the old wfLoadExtension( 'VEForAllMobileDeps' ); registration from the farm
settings for each affected wiki. Do not delete the old extension files while
the old registration is still active. On deployment, verify that both Minerva
Page Forms and desktop/Flow editors still load, edit and save correctly.

Page Forms VisualEditor content also receives 0.75rem horizontal padding,
matching the input-field spacing. This override is limited to #pfForm.

Parsoid API input protection
----------------------------

The veforall-parsoid-utils API requires POST; VEForAll already sends POST
requests from its editor. To avoid expensive unbounded conversions, inputs
are limited to 4 MiB by default (measured in UTF-8 bytes before parsing).
Change $wgVEForAllMaxConversionBytes in LocalSettings.php if your editor
fields require a different cap. Use 0 to disable the size limit. This is
a per-request size guard, not an API rate limiter.
